              <zone fixed-size='76' forceUpdate='true' h='10845' id='18' is-fixed='true' type-v2='text' w='98828' x='586' y='20429'>
                <formatted-text>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Book' italic='true'>Definitions and limitations</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Book' italic='true'>1/ Influencers are calculated based on selected date granularity. Filters won&apos;t influence the calculation</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Book' italic='true'>2/ </run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Book' italic='true'>Influencers</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Book' italic='true'> show how strong the selected dimension contributes to a total value of the selected funnel step. The higher or the lower % is the bigger the influence is. It&apos;s calculated as the difference between dimension funnel step value and total final step value and normalized by the amount of contacts handled in the selected dimension. 0% would often mean that the dimension has no effect on the total funnel step due to the small volume of contacts in that dimension.</run>
                </formatted-text>
                <zone-style>
                  <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                  <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                  <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                  <format attr='margin' value='4' />
                  <format attr='background-color' value='#fefaf1' />
                </zone-style>
              </zone>
